comments.message:
+1 Reading data.Roles from the Session resource is correct — roles are tied to the session, not looked up from AccountService users.

Suggest expanding the comment to note LDAP/certificate sessions may have Roles without a local user account. Sample:
```
  // Roles come from the Session resource. LDAP and certificate sessions
  // may have Roles without a corresponding AccountService user.
```

`userPrivilege` state stores the first entry from `Session.Roles` — a role name, not an AssignedPrivilege and not tied to a user account. Please add a brief comment here, e.g.:

  // First Session.Roles entry (role name). Session may be LDAP/cert without a local user.

Longer term, rename to `sessionRole` — see `usePrivilegeCheck.js` line 21 suggestion.
